// The EFFECT face of 00's root cause, and the reason the fuzzer could
// never find this class: the divergence is in stdout, which the trace
// oracle does not record. NOT ORACLE-VISIBLE — `graphix-fuzz check`
// reports AGREE on this program even while the bug is live (the values
// agree; only the guard's side effects differ). Reproduce by hand:
//
//   timeout 25 graphix --no-fusion 01_guard_effect_skipped.gx
//     G0 G1 G2 G3 G4 G5     <- arm 2's guard runs EVERY cycle
//   timeout 25 graphix 01_guard_effect_skipped.gx
//     G1 G3 G5              <- only cycles where arm 1's guard failed
//
// (the trailing `1 2 1 2 1 2` result lines are identical in both modes.)
//
// This also violates the emit contract in design/distributed_jit.md
// ("effects de-fuse, never silently skip"): the println inside the guard
// did not stop the select from fusing, and then half its executions were
// dropped. Whichever fix 00 takes (an unconditional guard prologue ahead
// of the if-chain), it must cover the effect too: a guard subtree
// containing an effect must be emitted unconditionally or de-fuse the
// whole select.
{
  let n = 0;
  select n { x if x < 5 => n <- (x ~ n) + 1, _ => never() };
  select n {
    x if x % 2 == 0 => 1,
    x if { println("G[x]"); true } => 2,
    _ => 3
  }
}
